  "notes": [
    "Regular reflexive -AR verb. Uses reflexive pronouns (me/te/se/nos/se) in all tenses. No stem changes or spelling changes.",
    "Regular past participle: *agarrado*",
    "Base verb: *agarrar* (to grab/seize something — non-reflexive). *Agarrarse* = to hold on, to cling to something.",
    "Often used with *a*: *agarrarse a la barandilla* (to hold on to the handrail).",
    "*¡Agárrate bien!* (Hold on tight!)",
    "*Se agarró al árbol para no caer.* (She held on to the tree to avoid falling.)",
    "Related: *agarrar* (to grab), *el agarre* (grip, hold)"
